            "review_text": "Wolf_Pack_SGN\nPerth, Australia2011 contributions\n0\nOrdered Delivery\nSep 2017 • Family\nI am not sure if this is just one of those places that you really need to eat at the restaurant. I ordered delivery and it was overwhelmingly underwhelming. After reading so many reviews about how good this place was, I decided to try it for delivery and it was so incredibly disappointing. \n\nThe \"char xiu\" is not like the typical hong kongnese type that you've come to expect when you utter the name. Usually you expect Chinese BBQ pork to be red honey glazed on the outside and usually relatively lean. The char xiu here is just like sliced pork pieces and very fatty without the distinguishing red colour around the edge of each slice of meat. \n\nThe duck was not very aromatic and to me, didn't even really taste like duck. Such an incredibly disappointing experience as I know District 5 is a bit of a distance, but I definitely had much better fresh hand made wontons from a lady at a street cart down the street from me that charges 20k for a won ton and noodle soup. My meal here really made me wish I had just walked the 100m to my local lady instead of ordering delivery from this place.\nRead more\nWritten September 17, 2017",
